[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Reachability note (important, and the reason this table is shaped this way)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The public ABI is exactly one function:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m int memchra2(int a, int b, int c, int d);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m It takes four plain `int`s — **no pointers, no lengths, no enums, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m out-parameters**. Every guarded helper is `static` and is called by `memchra2`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m with compile-time-fixed, always-valid arguments (a 64-byte local array that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `snprintf` always fills with at least `"test"`, a 4-element `int` array, string
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m literals, `count = 4`, `len = 4 == sizeof(int)`). Consequently **`memchra2`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m itself has no error return: it produces a defined result for every one of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2^128 input tuples.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows below are therefore split into two groups:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **E1–E14** — the C code's intrinsic rejection conditions. Each row records the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   trigger, the C result, and how the row is *observable*. Rows whose guard is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   unreachable from the public ABI are verified by asserting that the Rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `.so` takes the same *non*-rejecting path as the C `.so` (i.e. the guard must
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   be present-but-not-taken in both; if the Rust translation got a guard
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   backwards or dropped a `continue`, `memchra2`'s return value changes and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   differential test fails). The observable consequence is listed per row.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **B1–B7** — the generic FFI-boundary inputs that *are* reachable: extremes of
